    "teacher_markdown": "**What Students Should Take Away:**\r\n\r\n- Students use `groupby()`, `sum()`, and `unstack()` to organize existing passenger counts by class and satisfaction.\r\n- Students compare the satisfied and neutral-or-dissatisfied segments within and across airline classes.\r\n\r\n**Misconceptions Students Might Have or Points They Might Struggle With and Tips to Assist:**\r\n\r\n- Students may use `size()` instead of adding the values in `Count`.\r\n  - Tip: Explain that each row already contains a passenger count. `size()` would count rows, while `sum()` calculates the number of passengers.\r\n- Students may assume that the tallest bar represents the most satisfied class.\r\n  - Tip: Direct students to compare the individual satisfaction segments, not only the total height of each bar.\r\n- Students may treat “Neutral or Dissatisfied” as two separate categories.\r\n  - Tip: Reinforce that the dataset combines them into one category. AI Tutor can help explain the grouped output or chart code without answering the data question.",
